{"parentUuid":"f6ff6370-b04e-40d0-bce8-f1253f043372","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a4ecd78d0488484e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016LS5oUhji6uNeyytK4SKtF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" 9.15 sat_parameters new default symmetry_level probing site:github.com\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Parameter for symmetry finding dtime limit · Issue #4419 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4419\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.py at master · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/blob/master/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.py\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/symmetry.h at main · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/main/ortools/sat/symmetry.h\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/probing.h at stable\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/probing.h\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Presolve time limit · google/or-tools · Discussion #4280\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/4280\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at master · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT model that most of the time solved to optimality, but in rare cases it is determined to be infeasible · Issue #4839 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4839\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools: Google's Operations Research tools: · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools sat_parameters and symmetry_level. Here are the key findings:\n\nThe `symmetry_level` parameter has a default value of 2, as noted in the sat_parameters discussion. The symmetry_level can be set to 1 to only do symmetry breaking in presolve (with default 2 and also possible value 0).\n\nRegarding probing, the parameters include `probing_deterministic_time_limit` with a default of 1.0 and `presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit` with a default of 30.0.\n\nThe search results also indicate that OR-Tools version 9.15 introduced changes for converting integer values to enum values for parameters that require enums.\n\nFor more detailed information about specific changes in version 9.15 related to sat_parameters, you may want to check the official sat_parameters.proto file directly on GitHub at the google/or-tools repository.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"96493327-29b3-4038-82ff-cee265e852d5","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:35:55.431Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f6ff6370-b04e-40d0-bce8-f1253f043372","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2c87992b-e826-431b-96dd-f7ce0ac96e81","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a4ecd78d0488484e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FEn4zevvh527i6bdMos2EW","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Section from v9.15 Release Notes\n\nBased on the provided content, here is the complete CP-SAT section:\n\n**Improvements to the `no_overlap_2d` constraint** (presolve, propagation, and cuts).\n\n**Detect, store and use precedences** in presolve, propagation, and cuts.\n\n**Extensive work on LRAT proof production and checking.**\n\n**Improve linear1 and linear2 encodings and processing.**\n\n**Support for set variables and constraints** (experimental).\n\n**Extend support for enforcement literals to more constraints.**\n\n**Optimize Python layer, speed up proto generation, and improve typing support.**\n\n**Improve support for gil-less Python 3.14.**\n\n**Add soft constraint examples.**\n\n**Improve shared tree workers and clause sharing.**\n\n**Print solution on SIGTERM.**\n\n**Fix various bugs and improve heuristics.**\n\n**Improved scheduling cuts and memory management.**\n\n---\n\n## Analysis\n\nThe release notes provided **do not explicitly mention** any of the specific parameters you requested: `symmetry_level`, `ignore_subsolvers`, `cp_model_probing_level`, `fill_tightened_domains_in_response`, `repair_hint`, `FIXED_SEARCH`, or persistent hint behavior.\n\nThe only directly relevant feature identified is the enhanced `no_overlap_2d` constraint handling and improvements to shared tree workers, but no specific parameter changes or defaults are documented in this excerpt."}]},"uuid":"6db84a00-f040-4a9d-936f-9dcfdb852df7","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:35:56.049Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2c87992b-e826-431b-96dd-f7ce0ac96e81","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
