{"parentUuid":"f4b9579d-1979-4d0e-a251-07f16b9aa2a1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a4ecd78d0488484e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NFPJwfbxwQraf7jCPjTFdG","type":"tool_result","content":"# Analysis of sat_parameters.proto\n\n## Highest Field Number\n\nBased on the visible content, the highest field number appears to be **362** (mentioned in the file header comment \"NEXT TAG: 362\"), though the file is truncated and may contain higher numbers.\n\n## Recently Added/Experimental Fields\n\nFrom the provided excerpt, here are relevant fields with experimental or recent indicators:\n\n**Symmetry-related:**\n- No symmetry-specific fields visible in the truncated content\n\n**Probing-related:**\n```proto\noptional double probing_deterministic_time_limit = 226 [default = 1.0];\noptional double presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit = 57 [default = 30.0];\noptional int32 cp_model_probing_level = 110 [default = 2];\n```\n\n**Experimental flags visible:**\n```proto\noptional bool use_pb_resolution = 43 [default = false];\noptional bool expand_reservoir_using_circuit = 288 [default = false];\noptional bool inprocessing_use_sat_sweeping = 354 [default = false];\noptional bool interleave_search = 136 [default = false];\noptional bool detect_table_with_cost = 216 [default = false];\n```\n\n**LRAT Proof fields (recent additions):**\n```proto\noptional bool check_lrat_proof = 344 [default = false];\noptional bool check_merged_lrat_proof = 352 [default = false];\noptional bool output_lrat_proof = 345 [default = false];\n```\n\nThe content is truncated, preventing identification of fields specifically related to fill_tightened_domains, no_overlap_2d, or shared tree parameters."}]},"uuid":"91924d8a-2258-496e-8b74-f20c8ca17bbc","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:20.080Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f4b9579d-1979-4d0e-a251-07f16b9aa2a1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a015a200-0618-4719-9c72-1b6e4194944f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a4ecd78d0488484e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ARBqtUrUhc9xwvfe6L7z6B","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"or-tools CP-SAT bug fixed_search hint persistence 2026 issue\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the [hint] in the CP-SAT log\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/wsvOc-66-84\"},{\"title\":\"[CP-SAT] Search strategy to find all solutions, but fixing only some variables · Issue #1174 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1174\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Issue with Solution Hinting\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/8SemJDNHcTY\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT - Feasible hint not being used and solver doesn't find a solution\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/9fHmlUnITY4\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT and solution hints, though the specific bug about \"fixed_search hint persistence\" in 2026 was not explicitly detailed in these results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**CP-SAT and Solution Hints:**\n\nYou can inform CP-SAT about intuitions regarding the solution through hints, and some workers will try to follow these hints, which can significantly improve solver performance if they are good.\n\n**Known Issues with Hints:**\n\nThere have been reported issues where solution hints used as warm starts, even when complete and feasible, don't work properly. Additionally, hints containing duplicate entries can be a source of issues, and each variable index should only be hinted at once.\n\n**Hint Validation:**\n\nThe solver provides a `fix_variables_to_their_hinted_value` parameter for detecting infeasible hints, and while there's a `debug_crash_on_bad_hint` option, it's unreliable as it only triggers in multi-worker mode and depends on race conditions.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about a \"fixed_search hint persistence\" bug reported in 2026. If you're looking for a specific GitHub issue or release note, you may want to check the OR-Tools GitHub repository directly or provide additional context about the bug.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e3b443d4-44fd-451d-91c2-e39b4bff346b","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:21.047Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a015a200-0618-4719-9c72-1b6e4194944f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
