{"parentUuid":"1a841340-76fb-4790-b7c7-02cb743c8250","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a4ecd78d0488484e7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01R3bu3uUTysnmLBdimyoRPB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Critical finding: stable branch (= 9.15) NEXT TAG is 356; main branch is 362 → six new fields added post-9.15. R5/R6 said 9.15 had NEXT TAG=357/361 — those got cherry-picked into 9.15 itself. Let me identify the post-9.15 main-only fields (356-361)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2389,"cache_read_input_tokens":35654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2389,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CasscpVWvP98tdNhUimCR","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0934892b-b0fe-4c9e-80db-d921df0b1272","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:42.240Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0934892b-b0fe-4c9e-80db-d921df0b1272","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a4ecd78d0488484e7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01R3bu3uUTysnmLBdimyoRPB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WueFs93BgCCBntKRvYxW3E","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/or-tools/main/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto","prompt":"Find all proto fields with tag numbers 356, 357, 358, 359, 360, 361. For each, give the full field declaration including name, type, default, and any preceding comment block describing what the parameter does. These are post-9.15 additions and I need to know what each does."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2389,"cache_read_input_tokens":35654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2389,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CasscpVWvP98tdNhUimCR","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b010493f-f1d3-4fe7-b01a-f94148c1ab98","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:44.264Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b010493f-f1d3-4fe7-b01a-f94148c1ab98","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a4ecd78d0488484e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WueFs93BgCCBntKRvYxW3E","type":"tool_result","content":"# Proto Fields 356-361\n\n**Tag 356 - `num_ordering_in_vivification`**\n```proto\noptional int32 num_ordering_in_vivification = 356 [default = 1];\n```\nComment: \"The number of ordering to try each time we vivify a clause. This allow to spend more effort on vivivication if needed.\"\n\n**Tag 357 - `detect_encoded_complex_domain`**\n```proto\noptional bool detect_encoded_complex_domain = 357 [default = true];\n```\nComment: \"Depending on the model, a variable with a 'complex' domain like [0][2,5][7][9] is encoded... This presolve rule try to detect such case and remove these Booleans.\"\n\n**Tag 358 - `mip_scale_to_max_bound`**\n```proto\noptional bool mip_scale_to_max_bound = 358 [default = false];\n```\nComment: \"If true, both mip_var_scaling and mip_scale_large_domain are ignored. Instead, we scale any floating point variable by a power of two so that its domain is the largest that fit in [-mip_max_bound, mip_max_bound].\"\n\n**Tag 359 - `mip_presolve_restrict_bounds`**\n```proto\noptional bool mip_presolve_restrict_bounds = 359 [default = true];\n```\nComment: \"If true, use dual-reasoning to try to restrict the domains of the variable before we scale the model to integer. This can help with the scaling significantly.\"\n\n**Tag 360 - `cp_model_pure_sat_presolve`**\n```proto\noptional bool cp_model_pure_sat_presolve = 360 [default = false];\n```\nComment: \"Whether to use a simplified pure sat presolve only when cp_model_presolve is true. Crashes if the model is not pure SAT.\"\n\n**Tag 361 - `inprocessing_use_transitive_reduction`**\n```proto\noptional bool inprocessing_use_transitive_reduction = 361 [default = true];\n```\nComment: \"Whether we perform transitive reduction of the binary implication graph. This might reduce the number of implication significantly, but it might also loose some structure used by our detection algorithm like the logical gates detection.\""}]},"uuid":"7a553f44-3cba-4182-a704-b14d8f7a205c","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:36:52.424Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b010493f-f1d3-4fe7-b01a-f94148c1ab98","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7a553f44-3cba-4182-a704-b14d8f7a205c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a4ecd78d0488484e7","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GiirJMrGfYxT1er7hDjWCT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough data. Six post-9.15 main-only fields are all minor (vivification, MIP scaling, pure-SAT presolve, transitive reduction) — none touch our P0/P1 surface. Let me compile the report.\n\n## 1. 已发布版本时间线\n\n- **9.12.4544**: 2025-02-17\n- **9.13.4784**: 2025-06-06\n- **9.14.6206**: 2025-06-19\n- **9.15.6755**: 2026-01-14（PyPI 实际发布；GitHub tag 2026-01-12）— **当前最新**\n- **9.16+**: 不存在。R5/R6 当时预测的\"9.16 May release\"没兑现，Google 把功能直接合进 9.15（NEXT TAG 从原 R5 估的 357 推到 9.15 stable 的 356，9.15 实际涵盖了 R6 提到的 357/361 那批）\n\n## 2. 重要变化（影响项目）\n\n9.15 release notes 与 P0/P1 直接相关的就 3 条 high-signal：\n\n1. **`no_overlap_2d` presolve/propagation/cuts 增强**——我们 master_model 用 no_overlap_2d 做 70×70 网格摆放，这条**直接利好** P0 #1（exact 主体），无需配合，免费拿。\n2. **shared tree workers + clause sharing 改进**——影响 `num_search_workers + share_binary_clauses` 的并行行为；与 P1 #29 的对称性 + workers 配置耦合，升级后建议短跑 A/B 复测一次。\n3. **Print solution on SIGTERM**——168h campaign 的 wrapper 如果中途 timeout/被 kill，能拿到当前最优解；P1 #24 wrapper 可以受益（目前 SIGTERM 直接丢中间结果）。\n\npost-9.15 main 分支已合并 6 个新字段（356-361：vivification ordering、MIP scaling、pure-SAT presolve、binary impl 传递闭包等），全是 SAT/MIP 内部 presolve，**没有触及我们用的任何参数**。\n\n## 3. 升级建议\n\n**NO-GO（升级目标已经是当前版本）**——9.15.6755 == 我们装的版本，没东西可升。\n\n下一个动作点：盯 GitHub releases，9.16 真发布时再做评估（按 OR-Tools 节奏 6-12 个月，预计 2026 Q3-Q4）。\n\n## 4. 5 件套已落地配置 sanity check\n\n| 配置 | 9.15 status | 结论 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `symmetry_level=3` | proto 默认仍 = 2，level 3 仍是合法值；release notes 无 symmetry 默认变化 | 仍合理 |\n| `ignore_subsolvers` 6 项 LNS | shared tree clause sharing 改进可能影响其它 worker 的边际收益，但 ignore_subsolvers 黑名单语义不变 | 仍合理，建议下次 A/B 时复测 |\n| `cp_model_probing_level=3` | proto 默认 = 2，level 3 仍是合法上界 | 仍合理 |\n| `fill_tightened_domains_in_response` | 9.15 没动该字段；R5 调研结果继续有效 | 仍合理 |\n| `random_seed` override | 9.15 没动 search_branching/FIXED_SEARCH/random_seed 三件套 | 仍合理 |\n\n**额外提醒**：9.15 改了 `no_overlap_2d` 内部 cuts/presolve，过去用旧 9.14 跑过的某些 benchmark（cover_choice profile / presolve_log comparison）数字可能略有漂移；如果 P1 #20 路线图里要交叉对比历史数字，加一行\"OR-Tools 9.15 起\"的注脚足矣，不需要回滚或换版本。\n\n## Sources\n\n- [OR-Tools Releases · google/or-tools](https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases)\n- [ortools · PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/ortools/)\n- [OR-Tools v9.15 release tag](https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases/tag/v9.15)\n- [sat_parameters.proto stable (9.15)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [sat_parameters.proto main (post-9.15)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/main/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [Google for Developers — OR-Tools Release Notes](https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1215,"cache_read_input_tokens":38043,"output_tokens":1597,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1215},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1597,"cache_read_input_tokens":38043,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1215,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Casse4FXPeQ5dtWXS48ps","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c6d67c02-42f4-4d54-9292-33c434f6665d","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:23.331Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
